# Escape Room Project Structure Guide

This is a Next.js 15 escape room game with App Router architecture. Key files and directories:

## Core Application Structure

- [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx) - Root layout with Gaegu font and Korean language
- [src/app/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/page.tsx) - Landing page redirecting to start screen
- [src/app/start/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/start/page.tsx) - Player registration and session bootstrap
- [src/app/escape/[roomId]/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/escape/[roomId]/page.tsx) - Dynamic puzzle room renderer
- [src/app/finish/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/finish/page.tsx) - Leaderboard and completion summary

## State Management & Data

- [src/store/gameStore.ts](mdc:src/store/gameStore.ts) - Zustand store for game state (current room, hints, progress)
- [src/lib/rooms.ts](mdc:src/lib/rooms.ts) - Puzzle data and room definitions
- [src/lib/cardWords.ts](mdc:src/lib/cardWords.ts) - Card game word data
- [src/types/room.ts](mdc:src/types/room.ts) - TypeScript interfaces for Room and GameState

## Configuration Files

- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Dependencies and scripts (Node 22+ required)
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) - TypeScript config with @/\* path alias
- [tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js) - Tailwind CSS configuration
- [next.config.ts](mdc:next.config.ts) - Next.js configuration

## Assets & Media

- [public/images/](mdc:public/images/) - Room backgrounds (prefer WebP format)
- [public/assets/](mdc:public/assets/) - Game assets (sprites, textures)

## Development Commands

- `pnpm dev` - Development server with Turbopack
- `pnpm build` - Production build
- `pnpm start -- -p 10050` - Serve on port 10050
- `pnpm lint` - ESLint check
- `pnpm format` - Prettier formatting
